message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on Palsgaard ChoMilk 150, a stabilizer/emulsifier blend. Mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids, carrageenan, and guar gum together make a mixed preparation, which points to heading 2106 or 3824. Since it is a food additive blend, 2106.90 is likely. I recall rulings classifying similar stabilizer systems in 2106.90.99 (other food preparations not elsewhere specified).

The other candidates are 2106.90.9400 (other, dairy-containing) and 2106.90.9500 (other, not containing milk solids), among others. The statistical suffix 2106.90.9998 applies to "other" preparations not subject to quotas. Because the product contains no milk fat or sugar beyond dextrose as a standardizer, it would fall into 2106.90.9998 rather than the sugar-containing subheadings. Dextrose, a sugar, is present only as a standardizer, and the sugar-containing subheadings such as 2106.90.4200 and 2106.90.6000 apply to sugar-containing articles. Under 2106.90.66 (articles containing sugar described in additional U.S. note 3 to chapter 17), the sugar content is likely too low to matter. I therefore settle on 2106.90.9998.

{"hts_code": "2106.90.9998", "reason": "A stabilizer/emulsifier blend of mono- and diglycerides, carrageenan, and guar gum used as a chocolate milk additive is a food preparation not elsewhere specified or included, classified in the residual provision of heading 2106."}
